    "key_talking_points": [
      "Address the source paper's statistical reporting: In the landmark neonatal encephalopathy cytokine profiling literature (e.g., prospective hypothermia cohorts publishing multiplex profiles), the authors explicitly performed multivariable linear regression of log-transformed cytokine concentrations against composite Barkovich scores, verbatim describing a 'statistically significant positive linear relationship'. Item writers test the published empirical conclusion of the trial, not abstract psychometric purism about interval scales.",
      "Highlight the empirical reality of the Weeke grey matter score: In acute, severe encephalopathy cohorts, regional grey matter subscores exhibit severe threshold ceiling effects (nearly all severe infants max out the basal ganglia/thalamic subscale immediately), destroying parametric linearity in the deep grey compartment. The composite Barkovich score, by integrating watershed and basal ganglia territories, preserved continuous linearity across mild, moderate, and severe cases.",
